{"version":3,"term":{"cols":100,"rows":45},"timestamp":1790148387,"idle_time_limit":2.0,"command":".venv/bin/cortex-ask --real --tenant █████████ \"which stage are we losing the most deals at, by █████ and by value, and what does that tell us to fix?\"","title":"real_where_deals_die","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/zsh"}}
[0.0, "o", "Investigating REAL data for tenant \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: which stage are we losing the most deals at, by \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and by value, and what does that tell us to fix?\r\n\u001b[2m2026-09-23 12:56:29\u001b[0m [\u001b[33m\u001b[1mwarning  \u001b[0m] \u001b[1mmcp.nothing_admissible        \u001b[0m \u001b[36mlabel\u001b[0m=\u001b[35mposthog\u001b[0m \u001b[36mreason\u001b[0m=\u001b[35m'the server was queried and offered no tool Cortex can admit; every tool must declare readOnlyHint: true'\u001b[0m\r\nRead-only: no write capability exists in the tool registry.\r\nCapabilities available to \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: github, hubspot, posthog, slack\r\n  [  0.1s]          checking what data exists\r\n  [ 12.1s]          found posthog__list_projects\r\n  [ 12.1s]          checking memory for prior context\r\n  [ 17.3s] step 1   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 23.3s] step 1   calling hubspot__pipeline\r\n  [ 23.3s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 23.3s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 25.1s] step 1   got hubspot__pipeline (2 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 25.1s] step 1   got hubspot__search (3 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 25.1s] step 1   got hubspot__search (4 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 25.1s] step 2   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 27.3s] step 2   got read hubspot.search in full (100 rows) (4 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 27.4s] step 2   got read hubspot.pipeline in full (73 rows) (4 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 27.4s] step 3   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 68.6s]          drafting the report from 4 observation(s)\r\n  [ 99.9s]          checking every citation resolves\r\n  [100.0s]          re-reading each claim against its own evidence\r\n  sufficiency gate: skipped, this report asserts no cause (0.0s)\r\n  [110.6s]          writing the report\r\n\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Which stage are we losing the most deals at, by \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and by value, and what does that tell us to fix?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: low\r\nTook 100s over 3 steps, 63,889 tokens, 4 observations gathered, 2 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  The closed-lost deal records do not preserve which pipeline stage a deal was lost from \u2014 all \u2588\u2588\u2588 lost deals (2026-03-23 to 2026-09-23) simply show stage 'closedlost' \u2014 so the question as asked cannot be answered directly from this data.  [hubspot.search f988b039]\r\n  The recommended fix is twofold: instrument HubSpot to capture the stage a deal was in when marked lost (so this question is answerable going forward), and in the meantime, focus sales-ops attention on unsticking the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 deals stalled at presentationscheduled.  [hubspot.pipeline efa58664, hubspot.search f988b039]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Closed-lost deals do not record which stage they fell from  (high)\r\n    - All \u2588\u2588\u2588 deals matching the closed-lost filter for 2026-03-23 to 2026-09-23 carry stage value 'closedlost' with no prior-stage field, so it is not possible to determine which pipeline stage (e.g. qualifiedtobuy, presentationscheduled, contractsent) each deal was lost from using this data.  [hubspot.search f988b039]\r\n  Open pipeline shows deals concentrated and stalling at Presentation Scheduled  (medium)\r\n    - Several of the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st open deals by amount are stalled at 'presentationscheduled', including \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 ($\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588), \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 ($\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588), \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 ($\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588), and \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 ($\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588).  [hubspot.pipeline efa58664]\r\n  Closed-lost deal volume and value are concentrated in newbusiness deals sourced offline  (low)\r\n    - Among the \u2588\u2588\u2588 closed-lost rows read in detail, the great majority are labeled deal_type 'newbusiness' and source 'OFFLINE' with source_detail commonly 'INTEGRATION', 'IMPORT', or 'CRM_UI', suggesting most lost deals originated from outbound/offline sourcing motions rather than inbound web traffic.  [hubspot.search f988b039]\r\n\r\nHYPOTHESES TESTED\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  [inconclusive] Most deals are lost at the 'qualifiedtobuy' stage (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-stage disqualification) rather than later in the funnel.\r\n      Closed-lost records do not retain a prior-stage field, so this cannot be tested directly against the lost-deal data; the only stage-loss proxy available is the open pipeline's current stage distribution, which is not the same population as deals that were actually lost.\r\n  [inconclusive] Deals stall and are most likely to die at 'presentationscheduled', the stage holding the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and several of the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st-value open deals.\r\n      Presentationscheduled has the most open deals (\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588) and several six-figure deals sit there, which is consistent with it being a bottleneck, but this is a snapshot of currently open deals, not a measurement of where deals were before being marked lost, so it does not establish that this is where deals are actually being lost most.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  P\u2588 Add a 'lost_from_stage' custom property in HubSpot that is populated automatically when a deal is marked closed-lost, cap\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 the stage the deal was in immediately prior.\r\n      why: Without this field, stage-of-loss cannot be measured going forward, and this exact question cannot be answered rigorously today.\r\n      [hubspot.search f988b039]\r\n  P\u2588 Audit the \u2588\u2588 open deals currently sitting at 'presentationscheduled', particularly the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 ones (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 $\u2588\u2588\u2588k, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 $\u2588\u2588\u2588k, \u2588\u2588\u2588 $\u2588\u2588\u2588k, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588's $\u2588\u2588\u2588k), for stalled next steps.\r\n      why: This stage holds the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 of open deals and several of the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st dollar amounts, making it the most consequential bottleneck visible in the current pipeline even though it is not a direct measurement of historical loss.\r\n      [hubspot.pipeline efa58664]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - HubSpot's closedlost records overwrite the stage field to 'closedlost', destroying the information needed to answer the question directly (which stage deals were lost from). Any stage-of-loss conclusion here is inferred from the open pipeline's current distribution, not from actual lost-deal history, and could be wrong if deals lost \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 leave the pipeline faster than deals lost late.\r\n  - Only \u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 closed-lost deals were retrieved in full detail (\u2588\u2588 rows truncated); totals and stage/source distributions are based on the digest across all \u2588\u2588\u2588 for amount but full-row analysis only covers \u2588\u2588\u2588.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) were removed because an independent check found the cited evidence did not support them. Treat the remaining conclusions with corresponding caution.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and are retained with reduced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- executive_summary[0]: The evidence confirms total_matching=\u2588\u2588\u2588 and shows stage='closedlost' for the \u2588\u2588\u2588 returned records, but is truncated so the claim that 'all \u2588\u2588\u2588' show this stage is not fully verifi\r\n- findings[0].claims[0]: Only \u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 records are shown (truncated), so while all shown deals have stage 'closedlost' with no prior-stage field, this cannot be confirmed for all \u2588\u2588\u2588 deals from the trunc\r\n- findings[1].claims[1]: All four named deals (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 $\u2588\u2588\u2588k, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 $\u2588\u2588\u2588k, \u2588\u2588\u2588-\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 $\u2588\u2588\u2588k, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 $\u2588\u2588\u2588k) are confirmed at 'presentationscheduled' stage with matching amounts in the pay\r\n- findings[2].claims[0]: The truncated records do show deal_type mostly 'newbusiness' and source 'OFFLINE' with source_detail 'IMPORT' repeatedly, but the interpretive leap that this reflects 'outbound/off\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - Closed-lost deal search returned \u2588\u2588\u2588 total matching but only \u2588\u2588\u2588 rows in full detail; digest-level totals (sum $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588+) are based on the full population's amount field but per-row analysis covers only the \u2588\u2588\u2588 read.\r\n  - HubSpot deal stage is overwritten to 'closedlost' upon loss; no historical stage-at-loss field exists in the data available, so stage-of-loss must be inferred rather than measured directly.\r\n  - The github commits sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github deployments sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github issues sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github links sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog annotations sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog events sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  efa58664  hubspot.pipeline  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?open=true\r\n  f988b039  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closedate=2026-03-23..2026-09-23&hs_is_closed_lost=true\r\n\r\nphase breakdown (111s wall, 109s measured)\r\n  phase        calls  seconds  share    mean  tokens\r\n  survey           1     12.1   11%    12.1  in 0 out 0\r\n  recall           1      5.2    5%     5.2  in 0 out 0\r\n  loop_model       3     49.5   45%    16.5  in 6 out 4,118 cached 21,821\r\n  loop_tools       2      1.7    2%     0.9  in 0 out 0\r\n  draft            1     31.3   28%    31.3  in 56,886 out 2,879\r\n  gate             1      0.0    0%     0.0  in 0 out 0\r\n  verify           1      8.8    8%     8.8  in 29,449 out 1,273\r\n  sufficiency      1      0.0    0%     0.0  in 0 out 0\r\n  unmeasured              1.9    2%\r\n  cache hit rate: 20%\r\n"]
